<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<%- include(`${templatePath}/shared2026/head`, {
  headTitle: 'Converting Vrbo Partner Traffic into Rental Intent — Vicky Wang',
  headDescription: 'Reducing early-stage drop-off in a partner-entry mobile funnel with incomplete provider context.',
  headRobots: 'noindex, follow',
  headType: 'article',
  headImage: 'https://vickywang.me/thumbnails/cs_vrbo.png'
}) %>

<body>

  <%- include(`${templatePath}/shared2026/header`, {
    headerVariant: 'detail',
    headerHome: '/worklog',
    headerAvatar: '../../web_images/photo_profile_avatar.png',
    headerLinks: [
      { href: '#problem', label: 'Problem', muted: true },
      { href: '#insights', label: 'Insights', muted: true },
      { href: '#design', label: 'Design', muted: true },
      { href: '#impact', label: 'Impact', muted: true }
    ]
  }) %>

  <section class="cs-hero container cs-section--sm">
    <div class="cs-hero-meta">
      <span class="case-index">&#8470; 2 &middot; Q2 2026 &middot; BabyQuip</span>
      <span class="tag">DEMAND SIDE &mdash; SHOPPING</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="cs-h2 cs-h2--display">Converting Vrbo Partner Traffic into Rental Intent</h1>
    <p class="cs-hero-sub">Improving early-funnel progression across a constrained partner handoff.</p>

    <div class="cs-divider-grid cs-divider-grid--hero">
      <div>
        <div class="cs-stat-value">+60%</div>
        <div class="cs-stat-label">(22.6% → 36.1%)</div>

        <div class="cs-stat-label">Entry &rarr; Shopping progression</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="cs-stat-value">+52%</div>
        <div class="cs-stat-label">2.70% → 4.11%</div>

        <div class="cs-stat-label">Entry &rarr; Purchase progression</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-stat-note u-mb-sm">Matched 30-day GA4 pre/post comparison. Post period measured after launch stabilization and bug fixes. Directional; seasonality, traffic mix, partner-side changes, and post-launch fixes were not isolated.</div>

    <div class="cs-divider-grid cs-divider-grid--tight cs-divider-grid--bleed">
      <div>
        <div class="cs-label">ROLE</div>
        <div class="cs-text">UX designer for the 2026 redesign of the Vrbo partner-entry mobile web flow</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="cs-label">SCOPE</div>
        <div class="cs-text">Partner-entry funnel redesign &middot; Mobile web &middot; Consumer booking flow</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="cs-label">COLLABORATORS</div>
        <div class="cs-text">Design manager, CTO, engineering, QA, and growth/partnership teams</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-section--sm container">
    <div class="cs-kicker">CONTEXT</div>
    <div class="cs-two-col">
      <div>
        <h2 class="cs-h3">A two-sided marketplace, entered mid-journey</h2>
        <p class="cs-text u-mt-xs">BabyQuip is a two-sided marketplace where independent providers manage inventory, delivery, setup, pickup, and customer coordination. Its partnership with Vrbo launched in September 2025, bringing <strong class="cs-text-emphasis">high-intent, mobile-heavy traffic</strong> into BabyQuip's embedded mobile web experience, travelers entering mid-journey inside a constrained in-app browser, already committed to a trip but often meeting BabyQuip for the first time.</p>
        <p class="cs-text u-mt-xs">In 2026, Vrbo shared performance insights that revealed significant early-funnel friction. I was responsible for redesigning the partner-entry experience, Working with my design manager, I owned the redesign of covering partner entry, shopping, provider selection, and the handoff into checkout.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-media cs-ar-wide">
        <img class="modal-target" src="screenshot_Vrbo_BabyQuip.png" alt="Vrbo entry into BabyQuip" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-context">
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="problem" class="cs-section container">
    <div class="cs-kicker">01 &mdash; THE STRUCTURAL PROBLEM</div>
    <h2 class="cs-h2">An item-first experience built on provider-dependent fulfillment</h2>
    <p class="cs-lead">BabyQuip allowed travelers to browse and add gear before selecting a provider, even though price, availability, delivery, and fulfillment could not be confirmed until that provider was known.</p>
    <p class="cs-lead">Vrbo travelers entered this marketplace mid-journey, with their trip context already carried over, but the experience treated them like ordinary first-time shoppers.</p>
    <div class="cs-two-col">
      <div>
        <div class="cs-media cs-ar-standard">
          <img class="modal-target" src="screenshot_pricing_issue.png" alt="Placeholder pricing before provider selection" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-problem">
        </div>

        <br>
        <div class="cs-subhead">Marketplace-model mismatch</div>
        <p class="cs-text u-mt-xs">The interface supported item-first shopping, while fulfillment remained provider-dependent.</p>
        <ul class="cs-list u-mb-sm">
          <li>Travelers could browse and add gear before selecting a provider.</li>
          <li>Product information and prices appeared concrete during shopping.</li>
          <li>Final price, availability, delivery, and fulfillment were only confirmed after provider selection.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="cs-text u-mt-xs"><strong>The cart could feel real before the order was actually fulfillable.</strong></p>

      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="cs-media cs-ar-standard">
          <img class="modal-target" src="diagram_partner_entry.svg" alt="Placeholder pricing before provider selection" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-problem">
        </div>
        <br>

        <div class="cs-subhead">Partner-entry mismatch</div>
        <p class="cs-text u-mt-xs">Vrbo travelers arrived with a trip already booked, but often with little or no familiarity with BabyQuip.</p>
        <ul class="cs-list">
          <li>Their stay address and trip details carried over from Vrbo.</li>
          <li>They bypassed BabyQuip’s normal location-and-date entry gate.</li>
          <li>They entered directly into landing, shopping, or category pages inside Vrbo’s in-app browser.</li>
          <li>The product preserved their trip data, but did not clearly explain the handoff or how fulfillment worked.</li>

        </ul>
        <p class="cs-text u-mt-xs"><strong>They entered mid-journey with high intent, but without the context a direct BabyQuip visitor would normally build first.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-pullquote">
      <p>Together, these conditions created an experience that looked ready for shopping before travelers understood the partner handoff or the provider decision required to make the rental real.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="insights" class="cs-section container">
    <div class="cs-kicker">02 &mdash; WHAT THE DATA SHOWED</div>
    <h2 class="cs-h2">Users dropped before context, trust, and provider commitment were established</h2>
    <p class="cs-lead">GA4 and Hotjar showed Vrbo users were not primarily failing at checkout &mdash; they were dropping early, and the drop was concentrated on mobile.</p>

    <div class="cs-two-col">
            <div>
        <div class="cs-subhead cs-subhead--dark">Vrbo mobile vs. Vrbo web</div>
        <div class="cs-media cs-ar-portrait">
          <img class="modal-target" src="ga4_mobile_vs_web_traffic.png" alt="Vrbo mobile vs Vrbo web funnel comparison" data-modal-gallery="ga4">
        </div>
        <ul class="cs-list u-mt-sm">
          <li>Vrbo mobile progressed less effectively through the early funnel than Vrbo web.</li>
          <li>Because most Vrbo traffic arrived on mobile, the embedded experience was the highest-priority surface.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="cs-subhead cs-subhead--dark">Vrbo mobile vs. non-Vrbo mobile</div>
        <div class="cs-media cs-ar-portrait">
          <img class="modal-target" src="ga4_vrbo_nonvrbo_traffic.png" alt="Vrbo mobile vs non-Vrbo mobile funnel comparison" data-modal-gallery="ga4">
        </div>
        <ul class="cs-list u-mt-sm">
          <li>Vrbo mobile underperformed non-Vrbo mobile most sharply at entry into shopping.</li>
          <li>The primary weakness was early progression toward provider commitment, not checkout completion.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>

    <h2 class="cs-h2 cs-h2--follow cs-h2--sm">Four experience breakdowns that shaped the redesign</h2>
    <p class="cs-lead u-mt-sm">The early funnel drop was not caused by a single usability issue. It appeared as four distinct breakdowns, each pointing to a principle that shaped the redesign.</p>

    <div class="cs-breakdown-grid cs-breakdown-grid--two-col">
      <div class="cs-rule-top cs-rule-top--subtle">
        <div class="cs-breakdown-head">
          <span class="cs-breakdown-tag">A &middot; Entry confusion</span>
          <span class="cs-quote">&ldquo;Where am I?&rdquo;</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-media cs-ar-standard">
          <img class="modal-target" src="legacy_pre_entry.png" alt="Legacy Vrbo entry added friction before shopping" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-insights">
        </div>
        <ul class="cs-list u-mt-sm">
          <li>Blank loading state created uncertainty</li>
          <li>Multiple overlays competed for attention</li>
          <li>Chat blocked the primary CTA</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="cs-breakdown-principle"><span class="cs-principle-label">PRINCIPLE &mdash; </span><strong>Clarify context before action.</strong> Show where they are, what carried over from Vrbo, and why to trust the next step.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-rule-top cs-rule-top--subtle">
        <div class="cs-breakdown-head">
          <span class="cs-breakdown-tag">B &middot; Missing provider context</span>
          <span class="cs-quote">&ldquo;I thought these items and prices were confirmed.&rdquo;</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-media cs-ar-standard">
          <img class="modal-target" src="legacy_shop_placeholder_items.png" alt="Legacy shopping with generic products and pricing" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-insights">
        </div>
        <ul class="cs-list u-mt-sm">
          <li>Users added items before selecting a provider</li>
          <li>Starting prices masked provider-dependent pricing</li>
          <li>Shopping didn't naturally transition to provider selection</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="cs-breakdown-principle"><span class="cs-principle-label">PRINCIPLE &mdash; </span><strong>Reduce false certainty.</strong> Don't let the UI imply prices are final before the system actually knows them.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-rule-top cs-rule-top--subtle">
        <div class="cs-breakdown-head">
          <span class="cs-breakdown-tag">C &middot; Unclear next action</span>
          <span class="cs-quote">&ldquo;What do I need to do next?&rdquo;</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-media cs-ar-standard">
          <img class="modal-target" src="legacy_provider_selection.png" alt="Legacy provider selection lacked clear guidance" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-insights">
        </div>
        <ul class="cs-list u-mt-sm">
          <li>Add-to-cart feedback suggested completion</li>
          <li>CTA hierarchy favored continued browsing</li>
          <li>Provider selection wasn't presented as the next required step</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="cs-breakdown-principle"><span class="cs-principle-label">PRINCIPLE &mdash; </span><strong>Make commitment visible at the right moment.</strong> Guide users toward provider selection &mdash; the real commitment point.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-rule-top cs-rule-top--subtle">
        <div class="cs-breakdown-head">
          <span class="cs-breakdown-tag">D &middot; Repetitive checkout flow</span>
          <span class="cs-quote">&ldquo;Why am I doing this again?&rdquo;</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-media cs-ar-standard">
          <img class="modal-target" src="legacy_precheckout.png" alt="Legacy flow with repeated checkout states" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-insights">
        </div>
        <ul class="cs-list u-mt-sm">
          <li>Checkout and add-ons created repetitive loops</li>
          <li>Competing CTAs blurred the next step</li>
          <li>Users reached checkout before they were ready</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="cs-breakdown-principle"><span class="cs-principle-label">PRINCIPLE &mdash; </span><strong>Remove repeated decisions.</strong> Consolidate screens into one continuous path to checkout.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="cs-h2 cs-h2--follow cs-h2--sm">The synthesis: a mental model mismatch</h2>
    <p class="cs-lead u-mt-sm">Underneath all four breakdowns was the same thing: travelers expected one kind of experience, and the marketplace actually works another way.</p>

    <div class="u-mb-sm">
      <div class="u-mt-sm">
        <img class="modal-target" src="diagram_traveler_mindset.svg" alt="Traveler mental model diagram" data-modal-gallery="marketplace_traveler">
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="u-mb-sm">
      <div class="u-mt-sm">
        <img class="modal-target" src="diagram_marketplace_workflow.svg" alt="Marketplace workflow diagram" data-modal-gallery="marketplace_traveler">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-pullquote">
      <p>Users don't need to understand how this marketplace works. They may just want to <span class="accent">rent a crib</span>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="design" class="cs-section container">
    <div class="cs-kicker">03 &mdash; DESIGN</div>
    <h2 class="cs-h2">Solutions</h2>
    <p class="cs-lead">Because pricing and availability could not be finalized before provider selection, the redesign made that uncertainty visible through contextual messaging,instead of letting the UI imply false certainty.</p>

    <div class="cs-solutions">
      <div>
        <div class="cs-solution-head">
          <h3><span class="cs-solution-num">1 &middot;</span> Clarify partner context on arrival <span class="cs-solution-tag">Vrbo-specific</span></h3>
          <p>Replaced the blocking trip-details modal with lightweight confirmation messaging that preserved the traveler’s stay context and clarified the handoff from Vrbo to BabyQuip.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-breakdown-grid u-mt-0">
          <div class="cs-media cs-ar-portrait">
            <img class="modal-target" src="design_pre_entry01.png" alt="Privacy prompt" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-design-entry">
          </div>
          <div class="cs-media cs-ar-portrait">
            <img class="modal-target" src="design_pre_entry02.png" alt="Trip confirmation">
          </div>
          <div class="cs-media cs-ar-portrait">
            <img class="modal-target" src="design_pre_entry03.png" alt="Category entry" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-design-entry">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="cs-solution-head">
          <h3><span class="cs-solution-num">2 &middot;</span> Reduce false progress while shopping <span class="cs-solution-tag">Vrbo-specific</span></h3>
          <p>De-emphasized provisional pricing and reframed add-to-cart as a transition toward provider selection, rather than implying that the order was ready.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-breakdown-grid u-mt-0">
          <div class="cs-media cs-ar-portrait">
            <img class="modal-target" src="design_shopping01.png" alt="Placeholder pricing" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-design-shopping">
          </div>
          <div class="cs-media cs-ar-portrait">
            <img class="modal-target" src="design_shopping02.png" alt="Add-to-cart transition" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-design-shopping">
          </div>
          <div class="cs-media cs-ar-portrait">
            <img class="modal-target" src="design_shopping03.png" alt="Earlier provider guidance" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-design-shopping">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="cs-solution-head">
          <h3><span class="cs-solution-num">3 &middot;</span> Make provider selection the visible commitment point <span class="cs-solution-tag">Cross-platform</span></h3>
          <p>Elevated provider selection from a secondary option to the required next step, reducing cart states that appeared complete before fulfillment was confirmed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-breakdown-grid u-mt-0">
          <div class="cs-media cs-ar-standard">
            <img class="modal-target" src="design_select_provider01.png" alt="Clear next-step hierarchy" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-design-provider">
          </div>

          <div class="cs-media cs-ar-standard">
            <img class="modal-target" src="design_select_provider02.png" alt="Explicit provider commitment" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-design-provider">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="cs-solution-head">
          <h3><span class="cs-solution-num">4 &middot;</span> Remove repeated pre-checkout decisions <span class="cs-solution-tag">Cross-platform</span></h3>
          <p>Consolidated add-ons, order review, and checkout progression into one continuous path, removing repeated prompts to continue shopping or proceed.</p>
          <div class="cs-stat-note u-mb-sm">This case study covers the handoff into checkout; the checkout experience itself was redesigned as a separate project.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-solutions u-mt-0">
          <figure class="u-m-0">
            <div class="cs-media cs-media--diagram">
              <img class="modal-target" src="legacy_pre_checkout.png" alt="Before:Repeated branching and loops
" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-design">
            </div>
            <figcaption class="cs-media-caption"><strong>Before:</strong>Repeated branching and loops</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="u-m-0">
            <div class="cs-media cs-media--diagram">
              <img class="modal-target" src="design_pre_checkout.png" alt="After: One intentional path to checkout
" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-design">
            </div>
            <figcaption class="cs-media-caption"><strong>After:</strong> One intentional path to checkout</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="impact" class="cs-section cs-section--end container">
    <div class="cs-kicker">04 &mdash; IMPACT</div>
    <h2 class="cs-h2">What improved — and what the redesign revealed</h2>
    <p class="cs-lead">After launch, early-funnel progression and entry-to-purchase conversion improved directionally. The work also clarified the unresolved tension between gear-first discovery and provider-dependent fulfillment.</p>

    <div class="cs-two-col">
      <div>
        <div class="cs-subhead">Observed funnel changes</div>
        <p class="cs-text u-mt-sm">The strongest movement appeared at the stages targeted by the redesign: entry into shopping and progression from entry to purchase.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="cs-subhead">Simplify the path to checkout</div>
        <ul class="cs-list">
          <li>Consolidated the cart-to-checkout journey from three or four screens to two, removing repeated steps across platforms</li>
          <li>Improved the order summary and pricing breakdown so travelers proceed to checkout with greater confidence</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-block-divider">
      <div class="cs-heading-row">
        <h3 class="cs-h3 u-mb-0">Directional funnel gains, with the structural constraint still visible</h3>
        <p class="cs-text">Early-stage progression and entry-to-purchase conversion improved after launch. The results also confirmed that the deeper tension between gear-first discovery and provider-dependent fulfillment remained unresolved.</p>
        <span class="cs-meta">Pre-redesign baseline: <button type="button" class="cs-modal-link modal-target" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-ga4-launch">Mar 25 &ndash; Apr 24<img src="ga4_before_launch.png" alt="GA4 source · Pre-redesign baseline · Mar 25–Apr 24, 2026" hidden></button> &middot; Post-launch, stabilized: <button type="button" class="cs-modal-link modal-target" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-ga4-launch">May 17 &ndash; Jun 15<img src="ga4_after_launch.png" alt="GA4 source · Stabilized post-launch period · May 17–Jun 15, 2026" hidden></button> &middot; GA4, 30 days &middot; each Launch and stabilization period excluded.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-divider-grid cs-divider-grid--flush">
        <div>
          <div class="cs-stat-value--sm">22.6% <span class="accent">&rarr;</span> 36.1%</div>
          <div class="cs-stat-label">Entry &rarr; Shopping</div>
          <div class="cs-stat-delta">+13.5 percentage points · +60% relative lift</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-stat-value--sm">2.70% <span class="accent">&rarr;</span> 4.11%</div>
          <div class="cs-stat-label">Entry &rarr; Purchase</div>
          <div class="cs-stat-delta">+1.41 percentage points · +52% relative lift</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-divider-grid cs-divider-grid--tight">
        <div>
          <div class="cs-label">SUPPORTING</div>
          <div class="cs-text u-mb-xs">Shopping &rarr; Add to cart</div>
          <div class="cs-stat-delta cs-stat-delta--dark">34.4% &rarr; 36.3% <span class="accent">(+5.8%)</span></div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-label">SUPPORTING</div>
          <div class="cs-text u-mb-xs">Add to cart &rarr; Cart view</div>
          <div class="cs-stat-delta cs-stat-delta--dark">71.1% &rarr; 86.2% <span class="accent">(+21%)</span></div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-label">NOT COMPARABLE *</div>
          <div class="cs-text u-mb-xs u-color-faint">Cart &rarr; Checkout</div>
          <div class="cs-stat-delta cs-stat-delta--faint"> </div>
          <div class="cs-stat-note">Not directly comparable after launch. The redesign removed repeated cart and order-summary states, changing the meaning and frequency of checkout-entry events.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-stat-note cs-rule-bottom">Purchase volume also increased in the matched periods, but traffic, seasonality, and partner-side factors were not isolated &mdash; so it is supporting context, not a headline result.</div>

    </div>

    <div class="cs-two-col cs-block-divider">
      <div>
        <h3 class="cs-h3">Trade-offs</h3>
        <ul class="cs-list">
          <li>Provider-first vs. gear-first tension remained: travelers could still browse before fulfillment was confirmed</li>
          <li>Representative-item logic remained: final price and availability still depended on provider selection.</li>
          <li>Provider-first entry without selected items was explored but not shipped.</li>
          <li>Embedded webview and tracking limitations constrained measurement.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>
    <div class="cs-heading-row cs-block-divider">
      <h3 class="cs-h3 u-mb-0">Structural insight and future direction</h3>

      <p class="cs-text">A longer-term opportunity is a hybrid marketplace model that supports multiple entry paths while treating pre-provider gear selections as fulfillment requirements, not confirmed inventory.</p>

    </div>
    <div class="cs-two-col ">
      <div>
        <div class="cs-media cs-ar-standard">
          <img class="modal-target" src="design_dual-entry_model.png" alt="Start with gear or providers
" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-design-future">
        </div>

        <div class="cs-subhead  u-mt-sm">Start with gear or providers</div>

        <p class="cs-text u-mb-sm">Travelers could begin by browsing nearby providers or by describing the gear they need. Both paths would lead toward provider-specific inventory and fulfillment.</p>

      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="cs-media cs-ar-standard">
          <img class="modal-target" src="design_fulfillment_aware_discovery.png" alt="Select provider → see actual inventory and price" data-modal-gallery="vrbo-design-future">
        </div>
        <div class="cs-subhead  u-mt-sm">Match gear needs to eligible providers</div>
        <p class="cs-text u-mb-sm">Before provider selection, gear choices would narrow the providers capable of fulfilling the request rather than create a seemingly confirmed cart. After a provider was selected, the marketplace would reveal actual items, pricing, availability, and delivery options.</p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include(`${templatePath}/shared2026/footer`, {
    footerVariant: 'case-study',
    footerAllCaseStudiesHref: '/worklog',
    footerResumeHref: '/worklog/resume'
  }) %>

  <div class="wl-image-modal" id="wl-image-modal" aria-hidden="true">
    <button class="wl-image-modal__close" type="button" aria-label="Close image">&times;</button>
    <button class="wl-image-modal__control wl-image-modal__control--prev" type="button" aria-label="Previous image">&larr;</button>
    <figure class="wl-image-modal__figure">
      <img class="wl-image-modal__img" src="" alt="">
      <figcaption class="wl-image-modal__caption"></figcaption>
    </figure>
    <button class="wl-image-modal__control wl-image-modal__control--next" type="button" aria-label="Next image">&rarr;</button>
  </div>

</body>

</html>
